The Coranto logo (public/logo.svg and the images made from it) contains two
NASA images, both in the public domain: the Earth from NASA's Blue Marble
(NASA Earth Observatory) and the near side of the Moon from the Lunar
Reconnaissance Orbiter Camera (NASA/GSFC/Arizona State University). NASA does
not endorse Coranto.

The government aircraft list in the Watch Power lens is read at runtime from
the plane-alert database, (c) SDR-Enthusiasts, Ramon F. Kolb (kx1t) and
contributors, made available under the Open Database License:
http://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1.0/. It is not bundled.

The Relief lens reads, at runtime, forced displacement figures from the UNHCR
Refugee Data Finder (https://www.unhcr.org/refugee-statistics/) and Disease
Outbreak News from the World Health Organization (https://www.who.int). The
figures and notices are theirs and are shown as published. Neither is bundled.

The outlet ownership table (src/sources/news/ownership.js) comes from AUSPEX's
own table of outlets, (c) 2026 Connor Evans, Apache-2.0.

The atlas overlays (public/coranto-atlas/) come from AUSPEX: its country
table, city table, conflict list and disputed-line coordinates, (c) 2026
Connor Evans, Apache-2.0. Border shapes are from world-atlas 110m (ISC),
built from Natural Earth (public domain).
